WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:02.583 --> 00:00:05.791
Ser Jordan and the entire Dream Team are back!

00:00:05.791 --> 00:00:07.791
And they are going to destroy our realm

00:00:07.791 --> 00:00:09.333
one house at a time.

00:00:10.166 --> 00:00:12.791
Ser Jordan seeks to permanently end the debate,

00:00:12.791 --> 00:00:15.625
to prove he is the GOAT of GOATs

00:00:15.625 --> 00:00:18.000
It's no use. There's not a house in this realm

00:00:18.000 --> 00:00:19.375
that could beat the Dream Team.

00:00:19.375 --> 00:00:20.541
You're right.

00:00:20.541 --> 00:00:22.458
That's why we've got to build one.

00:00:22.458 --> 00:00:24.791
So, without further ado, I will announce

00:00:24.791 --> 00:00:26.500
the members of the Super Super House

00:00:26.500 --> 00:00:28.958
hereby known as the Knights of the Round Ball,

00:00:28.958 --> 00:00:31.791
as selected by the Maesters of the Mediadel.

00:00:31.791 --> 00:00:34.583
-Are you bloody serious? The Mediadel?
-What do they know?

00:00:34.583 --> 00:00:37.958
So where is this big battle supposed to take place?

00:00:37.958 --> 00:00:40.958
Tonight, we ride...

00:00:40.958 --> 00:00:42.083
for Seatttle.

00:01:00.000 --> 00:01:01.750
Men, our enemy doesn’t tire.

00:01:01.750 --> 00:01:03.250
They don’t manage their loads.

00:01:03.250 --> 00:01:05.125
Their fundamentals are perfect, 

00:01:05.125 --> 00:01:07.791
and they don’t get distracted 
by social media ravens.

00:01:08.166 --> 00:01:10.041
Expect relentless hand-checking

00:01:10.041 --> 00:01:12.000
and ruthless physicality.

00:01:12.000 --> 00:01:14.541
Not exactly your best pump-up speech there, Doc.

00:01:14.541 --> 00:01:16.125
How much practice time do we have?

00:01:16.125 --> 00:01:18.458
Our scouts say they’ll be here before dawn.

00:01:18.458 --> 00:01:20.166
Ugh. Look at this roster.

00:01:20.166 --> 00:01:22.875
They’re all masters of their positions.

00:01:22.875 --> 00:01:25.083
So we go positionless. It’ll confuse them.

00:01:25.083 --> 00:01:27.250
We’ve gonna have to be hyper efficient.

00:01:27.250 --> 00:01:29.416
Attack the rim or stay back behind the arc. 

00:01:29.416 --> 00:01:31.875
Rangers, let 'em fly from deep early.

00:01:31.875 --> 00:01:33.875
That’ll force them to respect our spacing.

00:01:33.875 --> 00:01:36.458
Yes, I will hit them with a barrage of step backs.

00:01:36.458 --> 00:01:38.916
And my passing ability will make them go

00:01:38.916 --> 00:01:41.958
“WOW! I’VE NEVER SEEN THIS FROM A BIG MAN.”

00:01:41.958 --> 00:01:43.375
And I’ll make sure to come up with some

00:01:43.375 --> 00:01:45.666
wily bullshit that will get them technical fouls.

00:01:45.666 --> 00:01:47.708
Right. You tell the refs the minute

00:01:47.708 --> 00:01:49.208
you see one of their tunics come untucked.

00:01:49.208 --> 00:01:50.416
We’ll need every edge

00:01:50.416 --> 00:01:51.666
we can get against the Dream Team.

00:01:51.666 --> 00:01:53.083
We could try going 2-3, 

00:01:53.083 --> 00:01:55.166
and force them into a long game of zones.

00:01:55.166 --> 00:01:56.166
Nope, '90s rules.

00:01:56.166 --> 00:01:57.333
That would be illegal defense.

00:01:57.333 --> 00:01:59.208
Crazy idea here, but uh,

00:01:59.208 --> 00:02:01.000
we could go small.

00:02:01.000 --> 00:02:02.000
Mike…no.

00:02:02.291 --> 00:02:03.083
Look, 

00:02:03.083 --> 00:02:04.625
we have the talent,

00:02:04.625 --> 00:02:06.250
we have the skills,

00:02:06.250 --> 00:02:07.708
and we have the strategy.

00:02:07.708 --> 00:02:10.583
But the reason I KNOW we will prevail

00:02:10.583 --> 00:02:11.583
is that we've got...

00:02:11.583 --> 00:02:12.375
the ultimate weapon.

00:02:14.708 --> 00:02:15.708
Analytics?

00:02:15.708 --> 00:02:16.708
No...

00:02:16.708 --> 00:02:17.583
You.

00:02:17.958 --> 00:02:18.833
Oh, yeah…

00:02:18.833 --> 00:02:19.750
no, I've got this...

00:02:20.583 --> 00:02:21.833
Go right for the heart. 

00:02:21.833 --> 00:02:23.541
You take Ser Jordan one-on-one

00:02:23.541 --> 00:02:24.833
and push his ass around.

00:02:25.458 --> 00:02:26.958
If he falls, they break.

00:02:26.958 --> 00:02:28.541
You want to prove you’re the GOAT?

00:02:28.541 --> 00:02:29.375
This is your chance.

00:02:30.458 --> 00:02:32.625
Yeah…yeah…no problem.

00:02:32.625 --> 00:02:34.625
I mean it’s just Michael Jordan, right?

00:02:35.666 --> 00:02:36.208
You know that?

00:02:36.208 --> 00:02:37.666
Will you excuse me for a second?

00:02:37.666 --> 00:02:38.791
I actually have to

00:02:38.791 --> 00:02:41.000
take my talents to the chamber pot...

00:02:41.000 --> 00:02:41.750
thanks.

00:02:43.541 --> 00:02:44.541
He’s got this.

00:02:46.833 --> 00:02:47.875
Hello everyone.

00:02:47.875 --> 00:02:49.416
Welcome to the first ever meeting of

00:02:49.416 --> 00:02:51.333
the Order of the All-Seeing Eye.

00:02:51.333 --> 00:02:52.541
Now, of course

00:02:52.541 --> 00:02:54.166
by “eye,” I mean “me.”

00:02:54.166 --> 00:02:55.166
I am all seeing.

00:02:55.166 --> 00:02:56.333
In case you didn’t know, I’m a genius.

00:02:56.333 --> 00:02:57.666
I invited you all here

00:02:57.666 --> 00:02:59.250
not because we’re friends,

00:02:59.250 --> 00:03:02.666
but because WE are part of a spiritual house,

00:03:02.666 --> 00:03:04.166
one built around our

00:03:04.166 --> 00:03:06.958
shared hatred of a common enemy. 

00:03:06.958 --> 00:03:07.666
Nik Stauskus.

00:03:07.666 --> 00:03:09.125
-KAT!
-Playing defense!
-Balls!

00:03:09.125 --> 00:03:09.791
Guys, no.

00:03:09.791 --> 00:03:10.333
Steph Curry?

00:03:10.333 --> 00:03:10.791
Kevin Durant.

00:03:10.791 --> 00:03:11.791
No. Guys, no.

00:03:11.791 --> 00:03:14.458
You're all here as victims of great snubbery,

00:03:14.458 --> 00:03:16.583
excluded from All-Realm teams,

00:03:16.583 --> 00:03:19.000
harassed by ignorant ‘fanlings,'

00:03:19.000 --> 00:03:21.000
chastised by analytics blog boys

00:03:21.000 --> 00:03:23.750
living in their parents’ dungeons.

00:03:23.750 --> 00:03:26.041
But let us wallow no longer

00:03:26.041 --> 00:03:28.083
in the backcourt of despair,

00:03:28.083 --> 00:03:31.708
for the shot clock on our slander nears zero.

00:03:31.708 --> 00:03:33.500
I have a dream,

00:03:33.500 --> 00:03:35.791
a vision of a Realm with no haters,

00:03:35.791 --> 00:03:37.291
no ‘hot takes’

00:03:37.291 --> 00:03:38.958
and no raven trolls

00:03:38.958 --> 00:03:40.958
sowing the seeds of disunity.

00:03:40.958 --> 00:03:42.625
A realm where we can just

00:03:42.625 --> 00:03:45.291
play basketball in peace.

00:03:45.291 --> 00:03:46.291
But first,

00:03:46.291 --> 00:03:50.083
we must destroy that which stands in our way:

00:03:50.458 --> 00:03:51.958
THE MEDIADEL!

00:03:51.958 --> 00:03:52.958
Here here!

00:03:53.583 --> 00:03:55.958
But isn’t the Mediadel too powerful? 

00:03:55.958 --> 00:03:57.291
What’s your plan, Kyrie?

00:03:57.291 --> 00:03:58.750
He doesn’t need a plan, Draymond.

00:03:58.750 --> 00:04:00.791
He’s an artist. He improvises.

00:04:00.791 --> 00:04:01.791
I’m an artist, Kevin.

00:04:01.791 --> 00:04:03.125
You never let me do what I want.

00:04:03.125 --> 00:04:03.958
Yes I did.

00:04:03.958 --> 00:04:05.791
I left that so you could

00:04:05.791 --> 00:04:07.041
take whatever stupid shots you please.

00:04:07.041 --> 00:04:09.125
This group is gonna destroy itself 

00:04:09.125 --> 00:04:10.666
before it destroys the Mediadel.

00:04:11.041 --> 00:04:12.333
Well then we better get started.

00:04:12.333 --> 00:04:12.958
Follow me.

00:04:17.666 --> 00:04:21.125
He went to the bench feeling heated

00:04:21.125 --> 00:04:24.416
Down from his post up high

00:04:24.416 --> 00:04:28.083
Over the boos of the crowd and the whistles

00:04:28.083 --> 00:04:31.375
They all heard his famous cry

00:04:31.375 --> 00:04:33.250
You can get two shots

00:04:33.250 --> 00:04:35.041
when a soft knight flops

00:04:35.041 --> 00:04:37.833
But a ball will never lie

00:04:37.833 --> 00:04:40.041
Poor Sheed can plead

00:04:40.041 --> 00:04:42.083
while the refs plays deaf

00:04:42.083 --> 00:04:47.250
That a ball will never lie

00:04:47.916 --> 00:04:49.541
That was actually quite good, Dame.

00:04:49.541 --> 00:04:51.250
Yeah, for a knight. Wow.

00:04:51.250 --> 00:04:52.916
Yeah, for a musician… 

00:04:52.916 --> 00:04:53.666
it’s not great.

00:04:53.666 --> 00:04:55.250
But for a knight… it’s pretty legit.

00:04:55.250 --> 00:04:56.500
Now Oladipo…whew!

00:04:56.500 --> 00:04:57.791
HE’S good for a bard.

00:04:57.791 --> 00:04:58.750
Like, he’s legitimately good.

00:04:58.750 --> 00:04:59.625
Indubitably. Oh my god,

00:04:59.625 --> 00:05:01.958
when he played Thingithmagigith on The Masked Singer?

00:05:01.958 --> 00:05:02.958
Oh my god, indubitably.

00:05:02.958 --> 00:05:03.583
Oh, yeah yeah.

00:05:03.583 --> 00:05:06.166
His voice is so good, it makes my arms blush.

00:05:06.166 --> 00:05:07.583
Alllllright…

00:05:07.583 --> 00:05:10.458
Well, if the Realm is ending tomorrow,

00:05:10.458 --> 00:05:13.000
I’ve got some things to take care of.

00:05:13.000 --> 00:05:15.250
James, you should get some rest.

00:05:15.250 --> 00:05:16.291
Are you going to bed?

00:05:16.291 --> 00:05:18.583
Uh, something like that.

00:05:18.583 --> 00:05:20.333
What was that about?

00:05:20.333 --> 00:05:21.333
He’s going to a brothel.

00:05:21.333 --> 00:05:22.000
Snitch!

00:05:27.000 --> 00:05:27.708
What it do?

00:05:27.708 --> 00:05:29.583
James, uh, wait up. Wait up!

00:05:39.000 --> 00:05:40.541
What in seven hells was that?

00:05:40.541 --> 00:05:41.833
I’ll tell you.

00:05:41.833 --> 00:05:42.666
Before Brooklyn,

00:05:42.666 --> 00:05:44.375
House Nets hailed from Jersey,

00:05:44.375 --> 00:05:46.291
but the fanlings were few,

00:05:46.291 --> 00:05:49.041
so the Lords of House Nets attempted a rebrand.

00:05:49.041 --> 00:05:50.458
They designed a new court,

00:05:50.458 --> 00:05:52.250
new tunics, armor and...

00:05:52.958 --> 00:05:54.458
a new mascot.

00:05:54.458 --> 00:05:56.875
But some thought this new mascot was just

00:05:56.875 --> 00:05:58.500
too cool.

00:05:58.500 --> 00:06:00.041
That the realm wasn’t ready

00:06:00.041 --> 00:06:01.625
for something so...

00:06:01.625 --> 00:06:03.625
totally radical.

00:06:03.625 --> 00:06:05.833
Swamp Dragons? That’s a myth.

00:06:05.833 --> 00:06:09.041
Is this another one of your conspiracy theories?

00:06:09.041 --> 00:06:09.875
See for yourself.

00:06:13.125 --> 00:06:15.250
Hey, Kyrie! What’s up? You’re back!

00:06:15.250 --> 00:06:16.916
Hey, you brought some cool dudes?

00:06:16.916 --> 00:06:17.916
'Sup, dudes?

00:06:17.916 --> 00:06:19.958
I hear you guys want to totally wreck the media.

00:06:19.958 --> 00:06:20.916
I'm down.

00:06:36.541 --> 00:06:39.541
Don’t show that kind of frustration 
in front of Ser Jordan.

00:06:40.000 --> 00:06:41.458
It’s like blood in the water.

00:06:41.708 --> 00:06:44.375
Oh. Looks like we’ve got a Jordan expert 
over here, eh?

00:06:44.666 --> 00:06:45.666
You could say that.

00:06:46.791 --> 00:06:47.416
Kobe? 

00:06:47.750 --> 00:06:49.708
I figured I could be of some service.

00:06:49.916 --> 00:06:51.958
Wait, you want to help us defeat Jordan?

00:06:52.541 --> 00:06:53.708
But you’ve always worshiped him.

00:06:54.041 --> 00:06:54.791
Aye.

00:06:54.875 --> 00:06:56.041
He inspired me,

00:06:56.166 --> 00:06:57.666
but I kneel to no man.

00:06:57.958 --> 00:07:00.250
I serve the good of the Realm. 

00:07:00.250 --> 00:07:01.250
You must continue 

00:07:01.250 --> 00:07:03.708
to move the game forward, King James.

00:07:05.666 --> 00:07:07.333
You are my legacy.

00:07:07.333 --> 00:07:08.500
Those knights in there,

00:07:08.500 --> 00:07:10.333
they are our legacy.

00:07:11.791 --> 00:07:12.625
I sense doubt.

00:07:13.583 --> 00:07:15.833
Look, I know I have the size,

00:07:15.833 --> 00:07:17.458
the skill, the power, but...

00:07:17.833 --> 00:07:19.166
this is Ser Jordan!

00:07:19.333 --> 00:07:22.500
I mean, the guy scored 38 points in the Finals

00:07:22.500 --> 00:07:24.333
when he had the PLAGUE!

00:07:24.416 --> 00:07:26.416
Yes, he’s a killer.

00:07:26.500 --> 00:07:27.833
And to defeat him,

00:07:27.833 --> 00:07:29.750
one must become a killer.

00:07:30.333 --> 00:07:31.791
Wait, what?

00:07:31.791 --> 00:07:34.458
Cut away all your distractions.

00:07:34.458 --> 00:07:37.750
Cut away self-doubt and insecurity.

00:07:38.166 --> 00:07:39.041
Once you have removed

00:07:39.041 --> 00:07:40.875
all that does not serve you in battle,

00:07:41.708 --> 00:07:43.500
you have found your mamba form.

00:07:45.291 --> 00:07:46.291
I’m sorry...

00:07:46.875 --> 00:07:48.250
I don't think I understand.

00:07:48.458 --> 00:07:49.458
I’m saying...

00:07:49.666 --> 00:07:50.666
